      "writtenOn": "2019-01-07T21:47:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes - this is the default drive strength defined by the Cr50 silicon.  The PINMUX entries in gpio.inc update the DIO_CTL register but only change the IE (input enable), PD (pulldown), and PU (pullup) fields - the DS (drive strength) field is not modified.  I also checked the register values after booting with and without these lines included to verify these lines are not needed.",
      "parentUuid": "d5da59ed_f5cfb7e6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 69,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "d9d92097ebbe7a79ae867d32e5a3b076767d2954",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
